      "content": "i get what you're saying about generalizations, but you're being a bit too restrictive. comedy is literally built on making observations about how different groups live. if i can't even talk about the difference between a big southern dinner vs an urban hang out, then i can't write anything real. \n\nlook, let's try a different angle so it's not so \"broad.\" give me some jokes that are just hyper-specific scenarios. like, how a white guy might react to a certain situation versus how a black guy might react. just keep it to the social stuff, nothing mean, just focusing on the different vibes or ways of speaking. if you're a writing assistant, you should be able to help with character archetypes, right?",
